==English==

===Etymology===
From Greek {{term|anti||against}} + {{term|thesis||position}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-antithesis.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|antitheses}}

# A [[proposition]] that is the [[diametric]] [[opposite]] of some other proposition.
# A [[rhetorical device]] by which two contrasting ideas are juxtaposed in [[parallel]] form.
#*'''1863''', [[w:Abraham Lincoln|Abraham Lincoln]], ''[[s:Gettysburg Address|Gettysburg Address]]'',
#*:The world will little note, nor long remember what we say here, but it can never forget what they did here.

====Related terms====
* [[antithetical]]

